                <pb facs="0577" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg481"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Buck.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 257.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch, No. 350, of the 7th ultimo, confirming your telegram of the 2d ultimo,
                    reporting the beaching of the United States transport <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan City</hi>, and giving further information on the subject.</p>
                <p>You will express this Government’s appreciation of the courteous aid tendered to
                    the vessel and her crew and passengers in the several quarters mentioned in your
                    dispatch.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
